   "channel_name": "SOIC",
   "description": "Could a slowdown in the AI trade bring foreign money back to India? And if Indian markets recover, will the same stocks lead the next rally?\n\nIn this Diwali special, Ishmohit examines the changing global market environment and why he is becoming more optimistic about India\u2019s prospects for 2027, while remaining cautious about the months immediately ahead.\n\nWe begin with the risks around AI infrastructure spending and what a slowdown could mean for Indian suppliers. There is another side to that argument: lower capital expenditure could improve cash flow for some of the large technology companies funding the build-out.\n\nThe discussion then moves to foreign institutional investors, the rupee and the possibility of capital returning to Indian markets. Why might large caps attract that money first? And why can Nifty rise while a small- and mid-cap portfolio struggles?\n\nThe thread connecting these questions is sector rotation. The businesses that led the previous bull market may not lead the next one. Ishmohit shares the areas he is researching, including capital markets, technology, pharmaceuticals, chemicals, music licensing and specialised manufacturing.\n\nWatch for the framework behind the outlook: how global capital flows, sector trends and individual businesses fit together, and what could change the investment case.\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nLEARN AND RESEARCH WITH SOIC\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n\nSOIC Membership\nLearn asset allocation, fundamental analysis, valuation, technical analysis, screening and industry research.\n[https://learn.soic.in/learn/SOIC-Course](https://learn.soic.in/learn/SOIC-Course)\nDiwali bonus: StockScans membership is included with SOIC Membership.\nUse code: DIWALI17\n\nStockScans\nStudy sectors, compare peers and screen businesses.\n[https://www.stockscans.in/home](https://www.stockscans.in/home)\nUse code: